<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0">
  <data key="d0">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 is Enapter's patented anion exchange membrane (AEM) electrolyser, a standardised, stackable and flexible system to produce on-site hydrogen. The modular design and advanced software integration allow set up in minutes and remote control and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057610</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter">
  <data key="d0">Enapter</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enapter is the organization associated with the patented AEM electrolyser, providing the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 and its technical information.&lt;SEP&gt;Enapter is the manufacturer associated with the EL 4.0 electrolyser, its patented anion exchange membrane technology, and Enapter EMS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anion Exchange Membrane (AEM)">
  <data key="d0">Anion Exchange Membrane (AEM)</data>
  <data key="d1">component</data>
  <data key="d2">Anion exchange membrane (AEM) is Enapter's patented membrane technology used in the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen is the product generated on-site by the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is the product generated by the EL 4.0 water electrolysis process, with production rate up to 500 NL/h, up to 1.0785 kg/24 h, and purity depending on output pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen (H2, CAS 1333-74-0, EC 215-605-7) is a compressed gas with purity ≥99.8%. It is extremely flammable, contains gas under pressure, and may explode if heated.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is the chemical substance identified by chemical name Hydrogen, chemical formula H2, CAS no. 1333-74-0, and EC no. 215-605-7. Hydrogen is a single substance rather than a mixture and is described as a high-purity compressed gas. Hydrogen is classified as Flammable gas Category 1 with H220 'Extremely flammable gas' and as Gases under pressure (Compressed gas) with H280 'Contains gas under pressure; may explode if heated'. Hydrogen is associated with asphyxiation in high concentrations, and the safety data sheet provides special firefighting advice and accidental release measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34cab1cc532ba23dc6d6b8a72f15de19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9e3002c421208587ad06d75543e1ad</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061959</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="On-Site Hydrogen Production">
  <data key="d0">On-Site Hydrogen Production</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">On-site hydrogen production is the process enabled by the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0, using the electrolyser to generate hydrogen at the point of use.&lt;SEP&gt;On-site hydrogen production is the application of the EL 4.0, a standardised, stackable, flexible system for generating hydrogen at the point of use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Required Hydrogen Flowrate">
  <data key="d0">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Required Hydrogen Flowrate</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The required hydrogen flowrate is the hydrogen production rate that can be achieved by stacking AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 units; no numeric value or unit is stated in the source.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Standby">
  <data key="d0">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Standby</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">Standby refers to the condition in which no hydrogen is being produced and the auxiliary components are not powered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auxiliary Components">
  <data key="d0">Auxiliary Components</data>
  <data key="d1">component</data>
  <data key="d2">Auxiliary components are parts of the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 that are not powered during standby.&lt;SEP&gt;Auxiliary components are parts of the EL 4.0; in the standby condition no hydrogen is produced and auxiliary components are not powered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057803</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modular Design">
  <data key="d0">Modular Design</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Modular design is a feature of the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 that supports stackable and flexible system setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057613</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Software Integration">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Software Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">controlsystem</data>
  <data key="d2">Advanced software integration is part of the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 system and allows setup in minutes and remote control and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057614</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remote Control And Management">
  <data key="d0">Remote Control And Management</data>
  <data key="d1">controlsystem</data>
  <data key="d2">Remote control and management is a capability of the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 enabled by advanced software integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057614</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Limits">
  <data key="d0">Battery Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Battery limits is a reference that should be checked for the complete requirements list for the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;Battery limits are referenced by footnote 2 in relation to the EL 4.0 maximum water input conductivity and the Owner's Manual.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Owners Manual">
  <data key="d0">Owners Manual</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Owner’s Manual is a document that should be checked for the complete requirements list for the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057615</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Complete Requirements List">
  <data key="d0">Complete Requirements List</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The complete requirements list is the full set of requirements for the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0, referenced in the Battery limits and Owner’s Manual.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057615</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S.E.P. Category">
  <data key="d0">S.E.P. Category</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">S.E.P. category is a classification to which the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 belongs according to Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU and Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057615</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU is the directive under which the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 belongs to S.E.P. category.&lt;SEP&gt;Pressure Equipment Directive 2014/68/EU is referenced by footnote 3 in relation to the CE mark conformity of the EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057798</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016">
  <data key="d0">Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016 is the regulation under which the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 belongs to S.E.P. category.&lt;SEP&gt;Pressure Equipment (Safety) Regulations 2016 is referenced by footnote 4 in relation to the UKCA mark conformity of the EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057798</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL Recognized Electrolyser Versions">
  <data key="d0">ETL Recognized Electrolyser Versions</data>
  <data key="d1">safetyrequirement</data>
  <data key="d2">ETL recognized electrolyser versions are the electrolyser versions accepted for the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;ETL recognized electrolyser versions are the versions for which ETL recognition is applicable, as noted for CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 conformity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057800</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Specifications">
  <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical specifications describe the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0; they are under continuous improvement and might be subject to change, so the website should be consulted for the most recent specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter AEM Electrolyser Website">
  <data key="d0">Enapter AEM Electrolyser Website</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enapter AEM Electrolyser website, www.enapter.com/aem-electrolyser, is the source to refer to for the most recent technical specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Improvement">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Improvement</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous improvement is the ongoing process affecting the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 product and its technical specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057617</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL">
  <data key="d0">ETL</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ETL is the organization or mark associated with recognizing electrolyser versions for the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;ETL is the organization whose recognition applies to electrolyser versions for CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 conformity; ETL recognition is limited to recognized electrolyser versions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057801</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stacking">
  <data key="d0">Stacking</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Stacking is the process of combining AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 units to achieve the required hydrogen flowrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057618</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Setup Time">
  <data key="d0">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Setup Time</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 allows set up in minutes due to its modular design paired with advanced software integration; no specific numeric value is given.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93ea68f378840f4523d46204f5b6f641</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057619</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 Technical Specifications (table)">
  <data key="d0">Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 Technical Specifications (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">Specification table for Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0. It lists hydrogen production up to 500 NL/h or 1.0785 kg/24 h, 35 barg output, 99.9% purity at 35 barg, 4.8 kWh/Nm3, 2.4 kW nominal, 3 kW peak, 0.3 kW standby, 420 mL/h water, IP20, 42 kg, and compliance/control details. It supports the surrounding claims of modular, stackable on-site hydrogen generation with remote EMS management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057669</data>
</node>
<node id="EL 4.0">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0</data>
  <data key="d1">equipment</data>
  <data key="d2">EL 4.0 is the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0, a patented anion exchange membrane electrolyser, described as a standardised, stackable, flexible system for on-site hydrogen production with advanced software integration and remote control. Specifications may change because the product is under continuous improvement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057784</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter EMS">
  <data key="d0">Enapter EMS</data>
  <data key="d1">controlsystem</data>
  <data key="d2">Enapter EMS is the energy management system used for fully automatic control and monitoring of the EL 4.0 via 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth and Modbus TCP over Ethernet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Water is a feedstock consumed by the EL 4.0 electrolyser, with consumption of approximately 420 mL/h at 25 °C and input pressure range of 1–4 barg.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is a suitable extinguishing media for hydrogen fires.&lt;SEP&gt;Suck back of water into the container must be prevented, and backfeed into the container must not be allowed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c202e5769aa4bdf573fb70310abc052a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-360cb75b7b6c18d60b1c4f91e5d2a671</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061222</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oxygen">
  <data key="d0">Oxygen</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxygen is an impurity monitored in the EL 4.0 hydrogen output purity specification, remaining below 5 ppm O₂ at both 35 barg and 8 barg conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Electrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Water Electrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">process</data>
  <data key="d2">Water electrolysis is the process used by the EL 4.0 to produce hydrogen, and is referenced in CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 for hydrogen generators using water electrolysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anion Exchange Membrane">
  <data key="d0">Anion Exchange Membrane</data>
  <data key="d1">component</data>
  <data key="d2">Anion exchange membrane is the patented electrolyser technology used in the EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057788</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cabinet">
  <data key="d0">Cabinet</data>
  <data key="d1">component</data>
  <data key="d2">The cabinet is part of the EL 4.0 enclosure and provides 6 U of internal space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057788</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EL 4.0 :: Production Rate">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0 :: Production Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 has a production rate of up to 500 NL/h, up to 1.0785 kg/24 h, equivalent to 0.5 Nm³/h.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EL 4.0 :: Hydrogen Output Purity">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0 :: Hydrogen Output Purity</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 hydrogen output purity is 99.9% at 35 barg with less than 1,000 ppm H₂O and less than 5 ppm O₂ at 25 °C; and 98.8% at 8 barg with less than 12,000 ppm H₂O and less than 5 ppm O₂ at 25 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057789</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EL 4.0 :: Output Pressure">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0 :: Output Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">operatinglimit</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL 4.0 output pressure is up to 35 barg.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b04ddc1618376e2d935f2885e7799a35</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792057790</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EL 4.0 :: Nominal Power Consumption per Nm³ of H₂ Produced">
  <data key="d0">EL 4.0 :: Nominal Power Consumption per Nm³ of H₂ Produced</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
