<node id="Hydrogen, Compressed">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen, Compressed</data>
  <data key="d1">substance</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen, compressed is the product name; chemical name Hydrogen; chemical formula H₂; CAS no. 1333-74-0; EC no. 215-605-7; INDEX no. 001-001-00-9; REACH registration is listed in Annex IV/V of Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 (REACH) and exempted from registration. The substance has a purity of ≥99.8%. It is classified as flammable gas (Category 1) with H220 and gases under pressure (Compressed gas) with H280. Identified uses include industrial and professional, aerosol propellant, balance gas for mixtures, calibration gas, carrier gas, chemical synthesis, combustion, melting and cutting processes, fuel cells, fuel gas for welding, cutting, heating, brazing and soldering applications, laboratory use, laser gas, process gas, test gas, consumer use, fuel gas, propellant gas, and shielding gas in gas welding.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen, Compressed is a flammable gas (UN 1049) that is stable under normal conditions, can form a potentially explosive atmosphere in air, and may react violently with oxidants.&lt;SEP&gt;HYDROGEN, COMPRESSED, UN 1049, Class 2.1, Label 2.1 Flammable gases, Classification Code 1F, Hazard No. 23, Packaging group None, Environmental hazards Not Applicable, Special precautions for user None. Transport restrictions: Passenger and cargo aircraft Forbidden and Cargo aircraft only Allowed. It has high volatility, contains greenhouse gas(es), can form a potentially explosive atmosphere in air, and may react violently with oxidants.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen, Compressed (UN 1049) is a compressed flammable gas. Its transport information is provided in Section 14. It is classified as a flammable gas (Class 2.1). Packaging group is None. Environmental hazards are Not Applicable. Special precautions for user are None in the table, but additional transport precautions are provided. It is forbidden on passenger and cargo aircraft but allowed on cargo aircraft only. Transport precautions include avoiding transport on vehicles where the load space is not separated from the driver's compartment; ensuring driver awareness of hazards; securing containers; closing and checking valves; using valve guards or caps; ensuring adequate air ventilation. Disposal: do not discharge into any place where its accumulation could be dangerous; cylinders should be returned to the supplier. The transport bulk statement (14.7) is Not Applicable according to MARPOL/IBC. Regulatory information includes Dangerous Goods Ordinance (Chapter 295) and Factories And Industrial Undertakings (Dangerous Substances) Regulation (Chapter 59AB). The SDS revision date is 28/11/2022.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c202e5769aa4bdf573fb70310abc052a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0c034b2641f77a2e80ced6c44548bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed4ba62bbb6bbb3cdf90d8cfba89dc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061994</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
