<node id="GHS/CLP Label Elements for Hydrogen, compressed (table)">
  <data key="d0">GHS/CLP Label Elements for Hydrogen, compressed (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">GHS/CLP label elements table for compressed hydrogen (CAS 1333-74-0) in SDS Section 2.2. It lists Danger signal word, H220 and H280 hazard statements, and precautionary statements P210, P377, P381, P403, with General and Disposal as None. It supports Section 2.1 classification and product identity, but it adds H280 and P381 beyond the surrounding excerpt and omits pictograms. The table is critical for communicating flammability, pressure, ignition, leak, storage, and ventilation safety information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-34cab1cc532ba23dc6d6b8a72f15de19</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061485</data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen Composition and Identification Table (table)">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Composition and Identification Table (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This one-row composition table in Section 3.1 identifies Hydrogen as the sole ingredient, with CAS 1333-74-0, EC 215-605-7, and purity &gt;=99.8%. It confirms the product is a single high-purity substance, supporting the surrounding hazard classification as an extremely flammable compressed gas and the regulatory identity details given for Hydrogen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d9e3002c421208587ad06d75543e1ad</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061485</data>
</node>
<node id="SDS Sections 12-13: Ecological Information and Disposal Considerations for Hydrogen, Compressed (table)">
  <data key="d0">SDS Sections 12-13: Ecological Information and Disposal Considerations for Hydrogen, Compressed (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This single-column SDS table presents Section 12 Ecological Information and Section 13 Disposal Considerations for HYDROGEN, COMPRESSED (UN 1049, Class 2.1). It reports no ecological damage, not applicable persistence, expected biodegradation, low pollution risk due to high volatility, and a greenhouse gas caveat. Disposal requires avoiding dangerous accumulation and returning cylinders to the supplier. It follows toxicology and precedes transport information, supporting the low-hazard environmental profile while noting greenhouse and explosive-atmosphere concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ed4ba62bbb6bbb3cdf90d8cfba89dc3</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061485</data>
</node>
<node id="SECTION 14: Transport Information for Hydrogen, Compressed (UN 1049) (table)">
  <data key="d0">SECTION 14: Transport Information for Hydrogen, Compressed (UN 1049) (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This two-column table presents transport classifications for hydrogen, compressed (UN 1049) across ADR/RID, IMDG, and IATA. It lists UN number, proper shipping name, hazard class/labels, packaging group, environmental hazards, and special precautions. Hydrogen is class 2/2.1 flammable gas, not environmentally hazardous, with no packaging group. Air transport is forbidden on passenger and cargo aircraft, allowed cargo aircraft only. It supports SDS Section 14 and surrounding transport precautions and regulatory context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792061485</data>
</node>
