<node id="ADR/RID">
  <data key="d0">ADR/RID</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">ADR/RID is the European Agreement concerning the International Carriage of Dangerous Goods by Road (ADR) and Regulations concerning the International Carriage of Dangerous Goods by Rail (RID). For hydrogen, compressed, it specifies UN Number UN 1049; proper shipping name HYDROGEN, COMPRESSED; Class 2; Label(s) 2.1: Flammable gases; Classification Code 1F; Hazard No. 23; Packaging group None; Environmental hazards Not Applicable; Special precautions for user None.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IMDG">
  <data key="d0">IMDG</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">IMDG is the International Maritime Dangerous Goods Code. For hydrogen, compressed, it specifies UN Number UN 1049; proper shipping name HYDROGEN, COMPRESSED; Class 2.1; Label(s) 2.1: Flammable gases; Packaging group None; Environmental hazards Not Applicable; Special precautions for user None.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062012</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IATA">
  <data key="d0">IATA</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">IATA refers to the International Air Transport Association regulations. For hydrogen, compressed, it specifies UN Number UN 1049; proper shipping name HYDROGEN, COMPRESSED; Class 2.1; Label(s) 2.1: Flammable gases; Packaging group None; Environmental hazards Not Applicable; Special precautions for user None. Additionally, passenger and cargo aircraft: Forbidden; cargo aircraft only: Allowed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Hazard Class">
  <data key="d0">Transport Hazard Class</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">Transport hazard class for hydrogen, compressed: ADR/RID specifies Class 2, with Label(s) 2.1: Flammable gases, Classification Code 1F, and Hazard No. 23. IMDG and IATA specify Class 2.1 with Label(s) 2.1: Flammable gases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Precautions for User">
  <data key="d0">Special Precautions for User</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">Special precautions for user for hydrogen, compressed are None in the table for ADR/RID, IMDG, and IATA. However, additional transport precautions are provided in Section 14.8: avoid transport on vehicles where the load space is not separated from the driver's compartment; ensure driver awareness of hazards; secure containers; close and check valves; use valve guards or caps; ensure adequate air ventilation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062015</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Passenger and Cargo Aircraft">
  <data key="d0">Passenger and Cargo Aircraft</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">For hydrogen, compressed, transport on passenger and cargo aircraft is Forbidden according to IATA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062016</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MARPOL/IBC">
  <data key="d0">MARPOL/IBC</data>
  <data key="d1">standard</data>
  <data key="d2">MARPOL/IBC regulations. For hydrogen, compressed, the transport bulk statement (14.7) is Not Applicable according to MARPOL/IBC.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062017</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flammable Gases Label 2.1">
  <data key="d0">Flammable Gases Label 2.1</data>
  <data key="d1">operatingparameter</data>
  <data key="d2">The hazard label for hydrogen, compressed is "2.1: Flammable gases", applied under ADR/RID, IMDG and IATA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7444e8b9cda5407aac838fe2176791cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Hydrogen_compressed_Datasheet.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1792062018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
