<edge source="SITRANS LH100" target="SITRANS LH300">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SITRANS LH100 and SITRANS LH300 share 4...20 mA communication, -10 °C to +80 °C medium temperature, ATEX/Exia/IEC Ex/EAC/UL/WRAS approvals, and ceramic diaphragms; they differ mainly in measuring span, accuracy, and long-term stability, with SITRANS LH300 positioned as the higher-accuracy submersible level sensor.</data>
  <data key="d9">comparison,shares_specifications</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a54c7cc3fd1b24440332f3b903c96434</data>
  <data key="d11">SITRANS-P-EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792059868</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SITRANS LH100" target="SITRANS P200/210/220">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SITRANS P200/210/220 differs from SITRANS LH100 by focusing on absolute and gauge pressure with a much wider pressure span and a wider medium temperature range.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,differs_from</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a54c7cc3fd1b24440332f3b903c96434</data>
  <data key="d11">SITRANS-P-EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792059870</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="SITRANS LH100" target="SITRANS FP differential pressure sensor">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">SITRANS FP differential pressure sensor is an outlier as a differential pressure sensor for flow measurement with flange-dependent temperature limits, materials including carbon steel and hastelloy, and special mechanical features rather than a simple transmitter span.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,differs_from</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-a54c7cc3fd1b24440332f3b903c96434</data>
  <data key="d11">SITRANS-P-EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792059874</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
